{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs26KurcQFUK6cVQsJCH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All three parts are in place, and both test files pass (63 tests). I did not commit anything.\n\n**What changed**\n\n- **`AgeFallback` enum** (`src/fromager/resolver.py`): `ALL`, `NEWEST`, `NONE`. `find_all_matching_from_provider()` takes `age_fallback` (default `ALL`) in place of the boolean. Each mode logs the exact message and level you specified on the `fromager.resolver` logger.\n- **Pin bypass**: if `provider.constraints.get_constraint(req.name)` is a single `==` specifier, age filtering is skipped and the INFO skip message is logged. This reuses the existing `_has_equality_pin()`, so wildcard and compound pins are still age-filtered. Range constraints still go through the filter.\n- **Bootstrap caller** (`src/fromager/bootstrap_requirement_resolver.py`): multi-version mode passes `AgeFallback.NEWEST`; single-version passes `AgeFallback.ALL`.\n- **Docstrings** on `find_all_matching_from_provider()` and the new enum are updated.\n\n**Tests**\n\n- `tests/test_cooldown.py`: the old `fallback_on_empty_age_filter=False` test now uses `AgeFallback.NONE`. New tests cover `NEWEST` keeping the single newest candidate, log levels for each mode, an exact pin skipping the filter, a pin outside the window still resolving under `NEWEST`, and a range constraint still being filtered.\n- `tests/test_bootstrap_requirement_resolver.py`: a parametrized test checks that multi-version passes `NEWEST` and single-version passes `ALL`.\n\n**Things to know**\n\n- One of my new assertions was wrong at first. `PyPIProvider` already applies the `==1.2.2` constraint during matching, so only 1.2.2 reaches the age filter. I corrected the expectation to `[\"1.2.2\"]`; the skip log confirms the new path runs.\n- `ruff format` reformatted one of the edited files, and `ruff check` passes. `mypy` is not usable here: `~/.local/bin/mypy` fails with `No module named 'mypy'` and the venv does not have it, so I did not type-check.\n- `tests/test_cooldown.py` showed as modified on disk partway through. I checked the diff and it matches only my edits."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8825,"cache_read_input_tokens":106706,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8825},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d4b7fea8-d4b1-487d-9bd5-56d0f80bb045","uuid":"f3298c9f-7a7b-48a7-bb9c-8aab820a7b21","timestamp":"2026-10-09T16:59:32.112Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs26KbWM97xMwyqcBExv"}
